    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0753" n="653" xml:id="pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860n.00/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Young</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-06T12:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 5:47 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>95. Serious situation arising in Lithuania from continued presence Bolshevik
                    troops and very active propaganda now carried on in all parts of the
                    country.</p>
                <p>All foreign representatives here agree that in general the situation throughout
                    Baltic Provinces is now much less favorable than short time ago. At this moment
                    the question is apparently largely as to whether Bolsheviks after finishing with
                    Poland will overthrow Baltic Governments by armed force and propaganda or
                    utilize Baltic states as intermediaries for trade purposes.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Young</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
